title: Add `pallet-assets-forwarder`
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Adds `pallet-assets-forwarder`, which lets any signed account replicate an asset of a local
    `fungibles` registry onto a sibling chain over XCM. The pallet reads the asset's minimum
    balance and sufficiency from the registry and sends the destination a `Transact` that
    force-creates the replica, owned by the pallet's sovereign account there. A permissionless
    `sync_asset_status` call re-sends the values after they change, and a manager origin can
    remove the local record and release the caller's deposit.

    The registry is any `fungibles::Inspect` implementation, so a single `pallet-assets` instance
    and a `fungibles::UnionOf` of local and foreign assets both work. `AssetIdToLocation` maps an
    asset id to its location from the sending chain's perspective, which is reanchored to the
    destination to name the replica. The pallet is pinned to XCM v5 and assumes the destination's
    `pallet-assets` instance is keyed by `xcm::v5::Location`.
crates:
- name: pallet-assets-forwarder
  bump: major
- name: polkadot-sdk
  bump: minor
